    "user_request_original": "Design a 12-layer planar multilayer dielectric film on Ge substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe, ZnS, ZnSe (12 finite layers total, alternating starting with ZnS at air interface). All 12 layer thicknesses are optimizable variables with bounds 300-1000 nm. Initialize thicknesses with linear geometric progression: layer 1 = 350 nm, layer 12 = 950 nm, intermediate layers linearly interpolated. Constrain optimizer maximum single-step displacement to ±80 nm per iteration. Use coherent TMM solver at normal incidence (0 degrees), unpolarized light. Spectral range: 3000-11000 nm with 2001 sample points. Objective: maximize average transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band while minimizing average transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. Total layer count fixed at 12 (within 16-layer manufacturing constraint). Materials resolved via registry (ZnS, ZnSe, Ge). Canonical user controls: wavelength intervals 8000-11000 nm, 3000-5000 nm. soft objectives: High transmittance in 8000-11000 nm band; Low transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. behaviors to suppress or avoid: High transmittance in 3000-5000 nm band. manufacturing constraints: Total layer count not exceeding 16.",
